2026-11-17 20:19:35 - Agent_20261117201220 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed CodeQL query UUID 20261117201013 which identifies lock operations without signal handlers for cleanup on process termination. Investigated 4 vulnerable locations across Unix and Windows file lock implementations:

1. src/filelock/_unix.py:48 - fcntl.flock in UnixFileLock._acquire() - no signal handler to release lock on SIGTERM/SIGKILL
2. src/filelock/_unix.py:63 - fcntl.flock in UnixFileLock._release() - no signal handler protection during unlock
3. src/filelock/_windows.py:34 - msvcrt.locking in WindowsFileLock._acquire() - no signal handler for cleanup
4. src/filelock/_windows.py:45 - msvcrt.locking in WindowsFileLock._release() - no signal handler protection during unlock

All 4 findings are true positives. The vulnerability is that if a process holding a lock is terminated by a signal (SIGTERM, SIGKILL, etc.), the lock is not properly released, potentially causing deadlocks or resource leaks for other processes trying to acquire the same lock. No signal handlers are registered to catch termination signals and perform cleanup (unlock and close file descriptor).
